@startuml mrta_mode_button_state_machine

title MRTA mode — server-side state machine (mrta_mode/server.py : MrtaMode)

skinparam DefaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam StateBorderColor #4A90D9
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #EAF4FF
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
skinparam NoteBorderColor #E0C060

[*] --> off

off : the resting state. A map click means\n"drive there" (plain PyDotBot).\nbots = null, detail = last reason (if any)
connecting : POST accepted (202). connect() runs on a\nworker thread: retries 10 x 1s for min_bots,\nbuilds a fresh WorldEngine + PIBT world
on : tick() loop running on its thread.\nA map click means "PIBT routes you there".\nbots = fleet size snapshotted at connect()
stopping : POST accepted (202). stop flag set ->\narrival wait woken -> tick thread joined ->\nPUT [] to every address in the snapshot

off --> connecting : POST /mode {on:true}
connecting --> on : connect() ok
connecting --> off : connect() fails\n(MRTAConnectionError,\nmessage -> detail)
on --> stopping : POST /mode {on:false}
stopping --> off : halt_all() done
on --> off : tick loop crashes\n(detail = "the planning\nloop stopped unexpectedly")

note right of connecting
  Rejected with 409 ("ask again next poll"): ANY POST while
  state is connecting or stopping. That refusal is what stops
  a double click from starting a second session on the same bots.
end note

note right of on
  A POST that matches the settled state (on while on, off while
  off) is a no-op, answered 202.

  No resume: every ON is a fresh PIBT world, so OFF then ON is
  how you pick up bots that joined after connect().
end note

@enduml
